\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Producer/consumer seam defects worked through in this paper. The split matters more than the count: the top three are \emph  {agreements} --- both sides consistent, both wrong --- which no parity test can detect, and which is why provenance rather than parity is the load-bearing instrument. The last row names parity's own limit: a harness that forces real perception every tick cannot see a defect that only exists on dream ticks.}}{7}{table.caption.15}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:defects}{{4}{7}{Producer/consumer seam defects worked through in this paper. The split matters more than the count: the top three are \emph {agreements} --- both sides consistent, both wrong --- which no parity test can detect, and which is why provenance rather than parity is the load-bearing instrument. The last row names parity's own limit: a harness that forces real perception every tick cannot see a defect that only exists on dream ticks}{table.caption.15}{}}
